Clippy wants to collapse the inner `if let Err` with the outer let-chain. But collapsing `if let Err(error) = writer.flush()` into the chain would bind `error` only on Err; the body uses error. Collapsed form:
```
if let Ok(mut guard) = self.file.lock()
    && let Some(writer) = guard.as_mut()
