{
    tracing::warn!(...);
}
```
That works with let-chains. Similarly the record() method has nested `if let Err` for writes but those are sequential statements inside the block, not a single tail if, so not collapsible (the first two are statements). The flush one is a sole inner if → collapsible. Let me collapse it.

